{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long LL;\nLL n,A[20],B[20],ans;\n#define FOR(i,a,b) for(int i=(a);i<=(b);i++)\n\nvoid dfs(int pos,LL now,LL res){\n//\tprintf(\"%d %lld %lld\\n\",pos,now,res);\n\tif(res>=ans)return;\n\tif(pos==0){\n\t\tif(!now)ans=res;\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\tint t=now/A[pos];\n\tint d=abs(t)-1;\n\tif(t<0)d=-d;\n\tint s=abs(t)+1;\n\tif(t<0)s=-s;\n\t// 72 -77 -66\n\tdfs(pos-1,now-t*B[pos],res+abs(t)*pos);\n\tdfs(pos-1,now-d*B[pos],res+abs(d)*pos);\n\tdfs(pos-1,now-s*B[pos],res+abs(s)*pos);\n}\nint main(){\n\tFOR(i,1,16)B[i]=B[i-1]*10+1;\n\tA[1]=1;\n\tFOR(i,2,16)A[i]=A[i-1]*10;\n\tscanf(\"%lld\",&n);\n\tLL m=n;\n\tint c=0;\n\twhile(m){\n\t\tc++;\n\t\tm/=10;\n\t}\n\tans=1e18;\n\tdfs(c,n,0);\n\tdfs(c,B[c+1]-n,c+1);\n\tprintf(\"%lld\\n\",ans);\n\treturn 0;\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Precompute arrays A and B up to index 20 (sufficient for 64-bit numbers)\n    B = [0] * 21  # B[0] = 0\n    for i in range(1, 21):\n        B[i] = B[i-1] * 10 + 1\n    A = [0] * 21\n    A[1] = 1\n    for i in range(2, 21):\n        A[i] = A[i-1] * 10\n\n    # Read input\n    n = int(sys.stdin.readline().strip())\n    m = n\n    c = 0\n    while m:\n        c += 1\n        m //= 10\n\n    ans = 10**18\n\n    # Recursive DFS\n    def dfs(pos, now, res):\n        nonlocal ans\n        if res >= ans:\n            return\n        if pos == 0:\n            if now == 0:\n                ans = res\n            return\n        # Integer division truncating toward zero (like C++ / for signed ints)\n        if now >= 0:\n            t = now // A[pos]\n        else:\n            t = -((-now) // A[pos])\n        # d = abs(t) - 1 with sign\n        d = abs(t) - 1\n        if t < 0:\n            d = -d\n        # s = abs(t) + 1 with sign\n        s = abs(t) + 1\n        if t < 0:\n            s = -s\n        # Recursive calls\n        dfs(pos - 1, now - t * B[pos], res + abs(t) * pos)\n        dfs(pos - 1, now - d * B[pos], res + abs(d) * pos)\n        dfs(pos - 1, now - s * B[pos], res + abs(s) * pos)\n\n    # First DFS using n itself\n    dfs(c, n, 0)\n    # Second DFS using complement to next repunit\n    if c + 1 <= 20:\n        dfs(c, B[c+1] - n, c + 1)\n\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.6954811548639555e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.0004323977918829769, -0.2086932361125946, -0.005234583746641874, -0.07903824001550674, -0.42572832107543945, -1.9851688146591187, -0.3869030773639679, -6.198863957251888e-06, -0.05046400427818298, -0.10854890942573547, -0.0002277830062666908, -0.7702494263648987, -0.7313420176506042, -0.0032660020515322685, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -0.06825745850801468, 0.0, -0.2674645483493805, -6.794906312279636e-06, -0.0001699779968475923, -0.08170746266841888, -3.7245917320251465, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -4.017272294731811e-05, -0.05841223